 2. ✈️ Google buying Spirit data to feed AI 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Google is paying $10 million for Spirit Airlines' business data to feed into its AI models, Axios' Nathan Bomey reports. 

 The trove includes emails, calendar info, chats, documents, spreadsheets and more. 🤑 Google won a bankruptcy auction for the data from Spirit, which stopped flying earlier this year after failing to emerge from Chapter 11 bankruptcy. 

 The data doesn't include any personally identifiable information, passenger profiles or frequent flyer info. 🤖 A Google statement says: "We acquired part of an enterprise dataset from Spirit Airlines, which can be helpful in improving our products and AI models."

 What's next: A federal judge still needs to approve the deal.

