 4. 📱 1 tech thing: Meet the fixable smartphone 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Image: Fairphone

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Dutch tech company Fairphone is bringing its owner-repairable smartphone to the U.S., Wired reports . 

 The Android phone ships with a small screwdriver. Users can order replacement parts — screens, charging ports, etc. — directly from the company. Fairphone CEO Raymond van Eck tells Wired: "If you look to the U.S. market, it's heavily duopolistic with very little real consumer choice."

 "Americans are exhausted by planned obsolescence, closed-box ecosystems, and expensive yearly upgrades." Learn more . 

 
 
